  "description": "DICZIA crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C218 H304 Co8 Gd6 N10 O54,7(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 4 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2A (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3A (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4A (Co) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 26 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.212-4.934 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 80.59-159.34°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C218H318Gd6Co8N10O61. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Gd(III), Co(II).",
